print(digits(4))  # Output: 0
print(digits(235)) # Output: 15
print(digits(12345)) # Output: 5
print(digits(123456)) # Output: 0
```

This function works by iterating through each digit of the number `n`, checking if it is odd, and if so, multiplying it to the `product` variable. If all digits are even, the product will be 0.
