You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a python function to set all odd bits of a given number. Your code should pass these tests:

assert odd_bit_set_number(10) == 15
assert odd_bit_set_number(20) == 21
assert odd_bit_set_number(30) == 31
[BEGIN]

answer:  def odd_bit_set_number(n):
    # Convert the number to its binary representation
    binary_representation = bin(n)[2:]
    
    # Iterate through the binary representation and set the odd bits
    for i in range(1, len(binary_representation), 2):
        if binary_representation[i] == '0':
            # Set the odd bit to 1
            n |= (1 << i)
    
    return n

# Test cases
assert odd_bit_set_number(10) == 15
assert odd_bit_set_number(20) == 21
assert odd_bit_set_number(30) == 31

print("All tests passed!")


