You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function of recursion list sum. Your code should pass these tests:

assert recursive_list_sum(([1, 2, [3,4],[5,6]]))==21
assert recursive_list_sum(([7, 10, [15,14],[19,41]]))==106
assert recursive_list_sum(([10, 20, [30,40],[50,60]]))==210
[BEGIN]

answer:  def recursive_list_sum(lst):
    total = 0
    for item in lst:
        if isinstance(item, list):
            total += recursive_list_sum(item)
        else:
            total += item
    return total

# Tests
assert recursive_list_sum(([1, 2, [3, 4], [5, 6]])) == 21
assert recursive_list_sum(([7, 10, [15, 14], [19, 41]])) == 106
assert recursive_list_sum(([10, 20, [30, 40], [50, 60]])) == 210

print("All tests passed!")


