You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a python function to set all even bits of a given number. Your code should pass these tests:

assert even_bit_set_number(10) == 10
assert even_bit_set_number(20) == 30
assert even_bit_set_number(30) == 30
[BEGIN]

answer:  def even_bit_set_number(n):
    # Convert the number to its binary representation
    binary_representation = bin(n)[2:]
    
    # Iterate over the binary representation and set every even bit
    for i in range(0, len(binary_representation), 2):
        binary_representation[i] = '1'
    
    # Convert the modified binary string back to an integer
    result = int(binary_representation, 2)
    
    return result

# Test cases
assert even_bit_set_number(10) == 10
assert even_bit_set_number(20) == 30
assert even_bit_set_number(30) == 30

print("All tests passed!")


