You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function to sort a list of elements using pancake sort. Your code should pass these tests:

assert pancake_sort([15, 79, 25, 38, 69]) == [15, 25, 38, 69, 79]
assert pancake_sort([98, 12, 54, 36, 85]) == [12, 36, 54, 85, 98]
assert pancake_sort([41, 42, 32, 12, 23]) == [12, 23, 32, 41, 42]
[BEGIN]

answer:  def pancake_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]
    return arr

