You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a python function to check whether the given number can be represented by product of two squares or not. Your code should pass these tests:

assert prod_Square(25) == False
assert prod_Square(30) == False
assert prod_Square(16) == True
[BEGIN]

answer:  def prod_Square(n):
    if n < 0:
        return False
    if n % 4 == 0:
        return False
    i = 1
    while i * i <= n:
        if n % i * i == 0:
            return False
        i += 1
    return True

