You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function to find the maximum sum of bi-tonic sub-sequence for the given array. Your code should pass these tests:

assert max_sum([1, 15, 51, 45, 33, 100, 12, 18, 9], 9) == 194
assert max_sum([80, 60, 30, 40, 20, 10], 6) == 210
assert max_sum([2, 3 ,14, 16, 21, 23, 29, 30], 8) == 138
[BEGIN]

answer:  def max_sum(arr, n):
    max_sum = 0
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i+1, n):
            if arr[i] < arr[j] and arr[j] < arr[i]:
                max_sum = max(max_sum, arr[i] + arr[j])
    return max_sum

