You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function to filter a dictionary based on values. Your code should pass these tests:

assert dict_filter({'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Kierra Gentry': 165, 'Pierre Cox': 190},170)=={'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Pierre Cox': 190}
assert dict_filter({'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Kierra Gentry': 165, 'Pierre Cox': 190},180)=={ 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Pierre Cox': 190}
assert dict_filter({'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Kierra Gentry': 165, 'Pierre Cox': 190},190)=={ 'Pierre Cox': 190}
[BEGIN]

answer:  def dict_filter(d, value):
    return {k: v for k, v in d.items() if v >= value}

