You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function to remove a specified column from a given nested list. Your code should pass these tests:

assert remove_column([[1, 2, 3], [2, 4, 5], [1, 1, 1]],0)==[[2, 3], [4, 5], [1, 1]]
assert remove_column([[1, 2, 3], [-2, 4, -5], [1, -1, 1]],2)==[[1, 2], [-2, 4], [1, -1]]
